n  (b * (a * b)) * a = ((a * b) * a) * b.\n  \\]\n  From Step 1, \\( (a * b) * a = b * a \\), so:\n  \\[\n  (b * a) * b = b * a \\quad \\text{(by idempotency)}.\n  \\]\n  Combining results:\n  \\[\n  a * b = b * a.\n  \\]\n  Thus, \\( * \\) is commutative.\n\n**2. Proving Associativity (\\( (a * b) * c = a * (b * c) \\)):**\n\n- **Step 4:** Start with condition (2):\n  \\[\n  (a * b) * c = (b * c) * a.\n  \\]\n  By commutativity (\\( b * c = c * b \\)):\n  \\[\n  (b * c) * a = (c * b) * a = a * (c * b).\n  \\]\n  Applying commutativity again (\\( c * b = b * c \\)):\n  \\[\n  a * (c * b) = a * (b * c).\n  \\]\n  Therefore:\n  \\[\n  (a * b) * c = a * (b * c).\n  \\]\n  This confirms associativity.\n\n**Conclusion:** The binary operation \\( * \\) is both associative and commutative under the given conditions. \n\n\\(\\boxed{\\text{The operation } * \\text{ is associative and commutative.}}\\)", "ground_truth_solution": "We are given a set \\( S \\) with a binary operation \\( * \\) such that the following properties hold: \n\n1. \\( a * a = a \\) for all \\( a \\in S \\).\n2. \\( (a * b) * c = (b * c) * a \\) for all \\( a, b, c \\in S \\).\n\nWe need to show that \\( * \\) is associative and commutative.\n\nLet's begin by demonstrating that the operation \\( * \\) is commutative.\n\n#### Step-by-Step:\n\n1. Consider any elements \\(a, b \\in S\\). Using property (1), we know:\n   \\[\n   b * a = (b * a) * (b * a).\n   \\]\n   \n2. Apply property (2) multiple times to transform the expression:\n   \\[\n   b * a = (b * a) * (b * a) = \\left( (b * a) * b \\right) * a.\n   \\]\n   \n3. Next, simplify the inner operation using property (2):\n   \\[\n   (b * a) * b = (b * b) * a.\n   \\]\n   \n4. Using property (1) on \\(b * b\\):\n   \\[\n   (b * b) * a = b * a.\n   \\]\n\n5. Substitute this result back into our earlier expression:\n   \\[\n   b * a = \\left( (b * a) * b \\right) * a = (b * a) * a.\n   \\]\n\n6. Apply property (2) again to rewrite \\((b * a) * a\\):\n  