). So no valid pairs. Similarly, \u5c71=5: \u7a77 + \u6c34=11 -5=6. Remaining digits:3,4,6,7. Possible pairs: 3+3 (invalid), 4+2 (used), 6+0 (invalid). Doesn't work. Similarly, \u5c71=6: \u7a77 + \u6c34=11-6=5. Remaining digits:3,4,5,7. Possible pairs: 3+2=5 (used), 4+1=5 (used). No. \u5c71=7: \u7a77 + \u6c34=11-7=4. Remaining digits:3,4,5,6. Possible pairs:3+1=4 (used), 4+0=invalid. Not possible. So if \u5c3d=8, then it seems impossible to satisfy the third equation. Therefore, \u5c3d cannot be 8.\n\nWait, maybe \u529b is 1 instead? Let's check. If \u5c3d=8, \u5fc3 + \u529b=3. If \u529b=1, then \u5fc3=2. Then \u5c71 must be greater than \u529b=1 but less than \u5c3d=8. So \u5c71 can be from 2 to 7. But \u5fc3=2 is already used. So \u5c71 cannot be 2. So \u5c71 must be 3-7.\n\nThen in the third equation: \u5c71 + \u7a77 + \u6c34 + 8 =19 => \u5c71 + \u7a77 + \u6c34=11. If \u5c71=3, then \u7a77 + \u6c34=8. Remaining digits: assigned digits are 8,1,2,3. So remaining digits:4,5,6,7. So \u7a77 + \u6c34=8. Possible pairs:4+4 invalid, 5+3 (used), 6+2 (used), 7+1 (used). Still impossible. If \u5c71=4: \u7a77 + \u6c34=7. Remaining digits:3,5,6,7. Possible pairs:3+4=7 (4 used), 5+2 (used), 6+1 (used). No. \u5c71=5: \u7a77 + \u6c34=6. Remaining digits:3,4,6,7. Possible pairs:3+3 invalid, 4+2 (used), etc. No. Similarly, no solution. So \u5c3d=8 doesn't work. So maybe \u5c3d=7.\n\nLet's try \u5c3d=7. Then first equation:2*7 + \u5fc3 + \u529b=14 + \u5fc3 + \u529b=19 => \u5fc3 + \u529b=5.\n\nPossible pairs for \u5fc3 and \u529b: since they are distinct digits from 1-8, not 7. Possible pairs:\n\n1+4=5\n\n2+3=5\n\n3+2=5\n\n4+1=5\n\nBut we also have the condition \u5c3d=7 > \u5c71 > \u529b. So \u529b must be less than \u5c71, which is less than 7. So \u529b can be 1,2,3,4,5,6, but since \u5c71 must be less than 7 as well. Wait, no: \u5c71 must be less than \u5c3d=7, but greater than \u529b. So \u5c71 can be from \u529b+1 to 6.\n\nSo \u529b can be from 1 to 5 (since \u5c71 has to be a